++# Research OS — Mission Control Phase 4A
++
++## Purpose
++
++Add a deterministic, read-only Mission Control projection over the existing `AgentRuntime` trace model. This is the first presentation-layer contract for an agent-native workspace and does not create a second execution authority.
++
++## Lifecycle view
++
++`goal -> plan -> tool/action -> result -> evidence -> decision`
++
++The current AgentRuntime trace provides high-level lifecycle events safe to expose: `run-created`, `planning`, `executing`, `verifying`, and `completed`/`failed`.
++
++## Authority boundaries
++
++- `FriendOrchestrator` remains execution authority.
++- `OwnerPolicy` remains authorization authority.
++- `ApprovalGate` remains approval authority.
++- `AgentRuntime` remains trace/lifecycle authority.
++- `MissionControl` is presentation/projection only.
++
++Mission Control must never execute a tool, authorize a tool, mutate a skill, change policy, or grant approval.
++
++## Owner isolation
++
++Snapshots are owner-scoped through `AgentRuntime.list_runs(owner_id=...)`. Individual run lookup verifies that the recovered run belongs to the requested owner.
++
++## Bounded projection
++
++Maximum snapshot runs: 100. Default snapshot limit: 25. Maximum events projected per run: 250. The projection reports truncation.
++
++## Explicit non-goals
++
++No browser automation, Windows input automation, tool execution, new permissions, MCP execution, provider-response persistence, dynamic UI code execution, or automatic promotion/release behavior.
++
++## Next increments
++
++1. Connect the projection to the desktop shell as a read-only timeline.
++2. Add structured goal/plan/tool/result/evidence/decision step categories.
++3. Add capability and tool-health panels using existing read-only catalog data.
++4. Add safe UI-schema validation before dynamic panels render.
++5. Keep every action behind the existing orchestrator/policy/approval gates.
